Z||000006||terryk||04-07-2001||12:33 PM||||That's entirely possible. I've just never measured the N car axles. You're in new territory but I trust CV Unlimited's knowledge. But what 4spd auto? It needs to be an E trans or the passenger side will be too long.<P>Yes, 97 is 65E. Only 96 had the Series II and 60E.<P>Terry<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||lowfunds||04-07-2001||09:23 PM||||Im not sure if it is a E trans or not thats why I wanted to get the measurements. CV unlimited said they should be the right size, when I asked if it would work. The gand am measurements are 20 1/2 to 21" drivers, and 21 3/4" in pass. So if anyone knew the measurements of the axles that work I could compare. Thanks <P>Matt<p>[This message has been edited by lowfunds (edited 04-07-2001).]||||reg||1
