Z||000013||rockcrawl||04-08-2001||08:39 PM||||Sorry I never got back to you with those measurements, I know I said I would. If yours is the '97 4T65E my measurements won't do you much good. The one I have sitting here is a 4T60E which I believe is shorter. I already have the axles installed wich makes it impossible to measure compressed length. Sorry.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I can measure the amount of exposed axle between the boots, but that probably won't do you any good.<P>If the GA has the same track width (hub to hub) and was available with the trans you are using, and has the same outer splines as the Fiero, then they should work without mod. ||||reg||1
